A host loads a linked extension through the file its link points at now.

Handed the link, jiti resolves the extension's own imports through the copy
it first loaded, so once a harness update moves the link and the old copy
goes, a hosted /reload fails with ENOENT on that copy's helpers. Only the
import takes the real path: the extension cache and the managed-proxy check
stay keyed by the link, and a reload's new cache token empties the cache.

--- a/packages/coding-agent/src/core/extensions/loader.ts
+++ b/packages/coding-agent/src/core/extensions/loader.ts
@@ -583,5 +583,8 @@
 	});
 
-	const module = await jiti.import(extensionPath, { default: true });
+	// pi-host: import the file the link points at now, so an extension whose
+	// link moved since the host started loads its new copy and that copy's
+	// helpers, rather than resolving them through the copy that's gone.
+	const module = await jiti.import(fs.realpathSync(extensionPath), { default: true });
